From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jxlarrea <jx@jxl.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gating: Report the ungated state after a short press

The Echo Show 8's privacy circuit ungates on any press of the button,
but the driver only told its listeners about presses of 500 ms or more.
After a short press ended privacy, the sound driver never heard that the
microphones were back, kept their enable line off and the microphone
FPGA lost its firmware, so every recording read zeros until a reboot.

When a short press finds the circuit ungated while the driver still has
it gated, report the ungated state as a long press would.
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/gating.c b/drivers/misc/gating.c
index 3e6364a3..89fd9236 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/gating.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/gating.c
@@ -180,8 +180,24 @@ static void handle_gating_button_event(struct gating_input_event *input,
 
 	delay = input->last_event_time + LONG_PRESS_DURATION;
 	/* if it is long press, it is a gating event */
-	if (!time_before(delay, jiffies))
+	if (!time_before(delay, jiffies)) {
+		/*
+		 * Any press ungates the circuit, a short one too. Tell the
+		 * listeners when that ended a gated state, or the microphones
+		 * stay off: only a long press told them before.
+		 */
+		mutex_lock(&priv->mutex);
+		if (priv->cur_state == GATED && priv->req_state == NONE &&
+		    __gating_state(priv) == UNGATED) {
+			priv->cur_state = UNGATED;
+			priv->req_state = UNGATED;
+			mutex_unlock(&priv->mutex);
+			schedule_work(&priv->priv_update);
+			goto out;
+		}
+		mutex_unlock(&priv->mutex);
 		goto out;
+	}
 
 	cancel_work_sync(&priv->priv_update);
 
